# shadcn/ui

All UI in this project is built with shadcn/ui. Components live in `src/components/ui/` and are imported via `@/components/ui/<name>`.

## Missing components

Before using a component, check whether `src/components/ui/<name>.tsx` exists. If it doesn't, install it with the shadcn CLI instead of writing it by hand:

```bash
npx shadcn@latest add button
```

- Use the kebab-case name from the shadcn docs: `npx shadcn@latest add dropdown-menu`.
- Several at once: `npx shadcn@latest add card dialog tabs`.
- Don't pass `--overwrite` unless asked; it discards local edits to that component.

## Usage

- Prefer existing shadcn components over custom markup or other UI libraries.
- These components are built on Base UI, not Radix. Use the `render` prop instead of `asChild`:

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<DialogTrigger asChild><Button>Open</Button></DialogTrigger>

// ✅ GOOD
<DialogTrigger render={<Button />}>Open</DialogTrigger>
```

- Style with Tailwind classes via `className`, and use theme tokens (`bg-primary`, `text-muted-foreground`) defined in `src/app/globals.css` rather than raw colors.

## Data Table

Data Table is not a CLI component. Use the shared `DataTable` in `src/components/data-table.tsx`, built on `@tanstack/react-table` v8 (v9 has an incompatible API).
